unreleased
  - Fall back to an in-memory database when a path can not be pread (such as a path inside a JAR on JRuby)

02-09-2026
  - Version 2.0.0
  - Require Ruby 3.3 or newer
  - Update the bundled MIME database from mime-types-data 3.2026.0701; some extension and content-type mappings changed to match current upstream priorities
  - Use byte offsets for reliable lookups in Unicode custom databases (#65, thanks @OskarEichler)
  - Avoid duplicate database reads for lowercase extension misses (#64, thanks @OskarEichler)
  - Preserve preferred extensions and extension-specific priorities when rebuilding the database (#66, thanks @OskarEichler)
  - Reload custom MIME databases when their configured paths change
  - Validate custom database row widths, row structure, and UTF-8 encoding

